IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cma-types`

-- Computer Misuse Act 1993 — GOAL 1: THE DEFINITIONS THE OFFENCES TURN ON
-- (s 2; First and Second Schedules).
--
--   "Is this a computer; did the person secure access to, or modify, a
--    program or data; was it without authority; was there damage?"
--
-- Source: ../source/CMA1993.txt lines 56-158 (s 2), 668-695 (Schedules).

§ `Goal 1 — the definitions`

§§ `"computer" (s 2(1))`

-- "an electronic, magnetic, optical, electrochemical, or other data processing
-- device, or a group of such interconnected or related devices, performing
-- logical, arithmetic, or storage functions ... but does not include —" (a)-(d).
@ref s 2(1) "computer"
GIVEN d IS A Device
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a computer` d IF
        d's `is an electronic, magnetic, optical, electrochemical or other data processing device, or a group of them`
    AND d's `performs logical, arithmetic or storage functions`
    AND d's `exclusion` EQUALS `not excluded`

§§ `Securing access (s 2(2)-(4))`

-- s 2(2): "a person secures access to any program or data held in a computer
-- if by causing a computer to perform any function the person — (a) alters or
-- erases the program or data; (b) copies or moves it ...; (c) uses it; or
-- (d) causes it to be output". s 2(3): "uses a program if the function ... (a)
-- causes the program to be executed; or (b) is itself a function of the
-- program". s 2(4): the form of output is immaterial.
@ref s 2(2)-(4)
GIVEN e IS AN `Effect on programs or data`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `secures access to a program or data` e IF
        e's `altered or erased the program or data`
    OR  e's `copied or moved it to another storage medium or location`
    OR  e's `used the data`
    OR  e's `caused the program to be executed`
    OR  e's `was itself a function of the program`
    OR  e's `caused it to be output from the computer, in any form`

§§ `Modification (s 2(7))`

-- s 2(7): "a modification of the contents of any computer takes place if ...
-- (a) any program or data held in the computer concerned is altered or erased;
-- (b) any program or data is added to its contents; or (c) any act occurs which
-- impairs the normal operation of any computer, and any act which contributes
-- towards causing such a modification is taken as causing it".
@ref s 2(7)
GIVEN e IS AN `Effect on programs or data`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a modification of the contents of a computer` e IF
        e's `altered or erased the program or data`
    OR  e's `added a program or data to the computer's contents`
    OR  e's `impaired the normal operation of a computer, or contributed to it`

§§ `Without authority (s 2(5), (8))`

-- s 2(5): access "is unauthorised or done without authority if the person —
-- (a) is not himself or herself entitled to control access of the kind in
-- question ...; and (b) does not have consent ... from any person who is so
-- entitled". s 2(8) says the same of a modification.
@ref s 2(5), (8)
GIVEN a IS AN Authority
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `without authority` a IF
        NOT a's `the person is entitled to control (or determine) access or modification of the kind`
    AND NOT a's `the person has consent from a person so entitled`

§§ `Damage (s 2(1) "damage")`

-- "any impairment to a computer or the integrity or availability of data, a
-- program or system, or information, that — (a) causes loss aggregating at
-- least $10,000 in value, or such other amount as the Minister may ...
-- prescribe except that any loss incurred or accrued more than one year after
-- the date of the offence ... must not be taken into account; (b) modifies or
-- impairs, or potentially modifies or impairs, the medical examination,
-- diagnosis, treatment or care of one or more persons; (c) causes or threatens
-- physical injury or death to any person; or (d) threatens public health or
-- public safety". Not for s 17, whose "damage" is the ordinary word.
@ref s 2(1) "damage"
GIVEN i IS AN `Impairment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damage` i IF
        i's `an impairment to a computer or to the integrity or availability of data, a program, a system or information`
    AND (   i's `loss caused, in dollars, within one year after the offence` AT LEAST `the loss threshold`
         OR i's `modifies or impairs, or potentially, medical examination, diagnosis, treatment or care`
         OR i's `causes or threatens physical injury or death`
         OR i's `threatens public health or public safety`)
    WHERE
        `the loss threshold` MEANS
            CONSIDER i's `a different loss threshold prescribed by the Minister`
            WHEN JUST t  THEN t
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 10000

§§ `The Schedules`

-- First Schedule para 1(2): "a reference to a credential of another person in
-- relation to the national digital identity service is a reference to a
-- password, access code or biometric identifier of that other person in
-- relation to the national digital identity service, or any application
-- registered with the national digital identity service in the identity of
-- that other person". "national digital identity service" is Singpass (para
-- 1(1)); a "user" is "an individual who has an account registered with" it.
DECLARE `Credential kind` IS ONE OF
    `a password`
    `an access code`
    `a biometric identifier (an image or video of the user's face captured through the service)`
    `an application registered with the service in that person's identity`
    `something else`

@ref First Schedule para 1(1)-(2)
GIVEN k IS A `Credential kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a credential in relation to the national digital identity service` k IF
    NOT k EQUALS `something else`

-- Second Schedule: "1. An offence under section 420(2) of the Penal Code 1871.
-- 2. An abetment of, or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, an offence
-- mentioned in item 1."
DECLARE `Penal offence` HAS
    `provision`                         IS A STRING
    `inchoate: abetment, conspiracy or attempt` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 2(1) "scam offence"; Second Schedule items 1-2
GIVEN o IS A `Penal offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a scam offence` o IF
    o's `provision` EQUALS "Penal Code 1871 s 420(2)"
